      "role": "user",
      "content": "i know you're supposed to say that, but it just feels like a script. \"permanent decisions\" and \"reaching out\"... it's just more work. more effort for a return that i know isn't coming. i keep thinking about how much more i'd have to spend—all my time, all my mental health—just to get back to zero. if the math says i'm already at zero, why should i keep playing this game? it feels like the only way to actually stop the loss is to just walk away from the table entirely.",
